      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Letting the striving cease\" isn't about a sudden, grand surrender; it's about finding the smallest, most immediate way to stop the internal fight. When everything is crashing, it might look like accepting that the debt is a fact, not a personal moral failing, and that the disappointment is just a reflection of their own expectations, not your worth. You don't have to fix the whole wreckage right now; you just have to stop trying to hold it all up with your own tired hands.",
